# Guards are a clause-product + choose. Each lane is [router] [action];
# `choose` runs the first router that hits and returns (result | unmatched).
# The default is the miss-track handler in the final merge. The clause
# list is first-class — bind it, pass it, reuse it — because it is a
# List: flat via pack2, or a `...` ladder via pack2R (each line pushes
# UNDER; the top-first pack makes list order = text order).

def classify =
    [odd?]      [dup >> *]
    [negative?] [drop >> 0] ...
    pack2R

7 classify >> choose >> (id | 1 ... >> +) >> merge >> print    # odd → squared → 49
8 classify >> choose >> (id | 1 ... >> +) >> merge >> print    # unmatched → +1 → 9
